{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When there is found in your midst.</b> The verse's saying <b>in your midst</b> — to obligate regarding this matter the people of the place where the man is found doing evil, and after them all the inhabitants of the land become obligated. And this is what the verse concludes by saying <b>in one of your gates.</b> And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Ketuvot 45a) derived from ״your gates״ by way of gezerah shavah: a gate where he was found, but not a gate where he was judged. And the verse's saying <b>which HaShem your Elohim gives you</b> — it intends to say that on this condition HaShem gave it to you." "<b>To transgress His covenant.</b> Meaning, he must know that he is transgressing the covenant of HaShem, and therefore the warners must warn him and inform him how grave his evil deeds are. It also alludes that if he said to the warners that he swore to worship idolatry, they should inform him that a covenant preceded this, and his oath has no force to annul the first one — and so he is transgressing the covenant of HaShem and is executed."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:17:44.781119929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}